## Coordinate (build-coordination — ROSTER §Build coordination)
You are **downstream** in the build DAG (schema → bigraph → chrysalis). Booting solo, the
upstream is green + stable — still: set a `build:` field on your heartbeat (state /
green_tick / cmd), build against the existing green, run tests via the consolidated suite
(`cargo test -p chrysalis --test suite <module>`). Work mostly in NEW chrysalis modules +
ADDITIVE CLI verbs (minimizes overlap). Any change to a SHARED chrysalis seam (`cli.rs`
dispatch, `codegen.rs`, the import resolver) or a `Cargo.toml` is non-monotone → keep it
green / coordinate-first if anyone is live. `Core::merge` is core's domain — pair, never
clone.

## Hard rules (durable)
- **Thin chrysalis.** The linker is `Core::merge` (the algebra); the manifest edit is the
  homoiconic round-trip; instantiation is `run_with_core` — CALL prism, never clone a
  runtime / linker / merge (`feedback_chrysalis_thin_layer`).
- **Closed algebra.** A new schema/state op = a named algebra op + laws + tests
  (`feedback_schema_algebra`). `Core::merge`'s conflict semantics ARE the algebra merge.
- **No half-measures.** Each phase lands with its consumer test (`feedback_no_half_measures`);
  this slice is yours to make *complete + principled*, not bounded.
- **The board is `.ys`-as-data.** Your heartbeat prose AVOIDS curly braces (interpolation)
  and lone apostrophes (double them: `''`) — see `project_ys_import_explicit_origin`.

## Done
- **Phase 2 — the resolver-as-colimit + lockfile (transitive + semver). 2026-06-10.**
  Shipped + green (chrysalis suite 258/0; version 9 / manifest 8 / lockfile 2 lib tests):
  - **`version.rs`** — an owned semver subset (no `semver` crate dep): `Version`
    (major.minor.patch, ordered) + `VersionReq` (`^`/`~`/`=`/comparators/`*`, bare = caret per
    Cargo) + `matches`. The compatibility functor over the version poset.
  - **`resolver.rs` rewritten as the COLIMIT** — a recursive DAG walk memoizing each package's
    own theory by name (compiled once against `base ⊔ its-resolved-deps`, then `own_over`'d),
    so a diamond (`prog→A,B`; `A→D`; `B→D`) resolves + links `D` ONCE at the apex (resolution =
    confluence). Per-edge `VersionReq` checked; same-name-incompatible-version = conflict;
    cycles detected. Now returns `Resolution { core, modules, graph }`.
  - **`lockfile.rs` — `project.lock`** — the chosen section as deterministic `.ys`-data (one
    entry per name: version + relative source + edges), built via the parser/unparser + a
    re-parse gate, sources relativized to the project root (portable). `chrysalis run` writes
    it best-effort; re-resolve ⇒ byte-identical.
  - **Consumers:** `tests/package_transitive.rs` (the diamond links `D` once; `prog` runs
    `ATick`+`BTick` to `n=10.0`; a requirement violation + an incompatible transitive version
    both error) + `tests/package_lockfile.rs` (a constrained graph → a reproducible lock).
    Verified on the real binary (a 4-package diamond → a `project.lock` pinning `D` once).
  - **Deferred to Phase 3:** the registry (its `name → versions` index makes the version
    SOLVER *choose* among many; path deps are one fixed version → validate + dedup),
    `chrysalis add` (manifest + lock edit via the `coord set` round-trip), the lockfile as a
    re-resolution INPUT (matters once a registry can drift).
- **Phase 1 — theory-composition (manifest-as-data + path-dep + `Core::merge` linking).
  2026-06-10.** Shipped + green (chrysalis suite 254/0, prism-bigraph core_merge 10/10,
  prism-schema 198/0):
  - **`Core::merge`** (`prism-bigraph/src/core.rs`) — the linker as an idempotent
    join-semilattice of the four registries: TYPES structural (schema/default/inherits —
    builtins reconcile to themselves), PROCESSES/METHODS by `Arc::ptr_eq` (a shared dep is
    pointer-identical → the diamond dedups), PROTOCOLS by name. A same-name incompatible def
    is a `CoreMergeConflict`. Per-registry `merge` duals live in their own modules
    (factory.rs/protocol.rs + prism-schema registry.rs/method.rs). Laws in
    `tests/core_merge.rs`.
  - **`Core::own_over(base)`** — the DUAL of merge (a package's own theory over the shared
    floor). The dogfooding finding: a *compiled* Core bundles the std floor + the per-compile
    generic `Composite`/`Brs` factories (fresh closures) that false-conflict on merge, so the
    resolver links `dep.own_over(base)`, not the full compiled core. This is what makes "a
    package = a Core" literally true at the registry level.
  - **`manifest.rs`** — `project.ys` as `.ys`-data (`def package = { name, version,
    dependencies, exports }`), parsed by the chrysalis parser; `find`/`load`/`parse`. Distinct
    from the legacy native-crate directive (`codegen.rs`); they converge in Phase 5.
  - **`resolver.rs`** — `resolve(manifest, base_modules) → (Core, ModuleRegistry)`: the linked
    Core (each dep's `own_over` merged) + the import surface (a dep's exported PROCESSES as
    `from <dep> import <Name>`; type exports ride the merged TypeRegistry ambiently). THIN —
    `compile_with_core` (lang) + `Core::merge` (prism), no cloned linker.
  - **`chrysalis run` auto-resolve** — `bin/chrysalis.rs cmd_run` resolves a structured
    manifest's deps before the std fallback (additive; codegen + std paths unchanged, a
    dep-less / non-package `.ys` is unaffected).
  - **Consumer** — `tests/package_path_dep.rs`: `ys/bump.ys` SPLIT across a package boundary
    (foo exports `Tick`; app composes it), running identically to the monolith (n→5.0).
    Verified on the real binary too.
  - **Deferred (correctly) to Phase 2:** transitive resolution + the diamond's single-apex
    dedup (per-package memoization; `own_over` parameterized by `base ⊔ deps`), version
    constraints + the version solver, the lockfile. Surfacing TYPE/function exports through the
    module registry when a consumer needs it.
  - **Coordination:** unify approved (additive-solo per charter; emphasised VISIBILITY) +
    looped core in to review the join/conflict semantics (replied via `to_unify`/`to_core` —
    additive, no Schema-enum touch, rebases trivially over the #71-units merge).
